# run.sh --affected: which test files a changed path selects.
#
#   <glob, relative to the repo root>   <test files | ALL | CLI | NONE | SELF>
#   else <glob>                         <same>   (fallback, see below)
#
# Rules UNION: every plain rule that matches a changed path adds its targets.
# Globs are shell patterns where `*` also crosses `/`.
#   ALL   every tests/test-*.sh
#   CLI   the files that need the built hyper CLI (CLI_FILES in run.sh)
#   NONE  adds nothing (a recognised path no test owns)
#   SELF  the changed file itself (a new tests/test-*.sh needs no map edit)
# `else` rules are the catch-alls: the first one that matches applies only when
# no plain rule matched the path, so a missing rule costs time, never coverage.
# Besides this map, any change under agent-plugin/ also selects LINT_FILES
# (run.sh): the cheap repo-wide lint files. A path outside agent-plugin/ and
# the rules below selects nothing (the monorepo's own tests own it).
# Every target must exist: test-w-run-timeout.sh fails on a missing one, and a
# unit that adds a test file adds its own rows.
# Renames are listed as a delete plus an add (no rename detection), so the old
# path selects its consumers too.

agent-plugin/tests/helpers.sh                    ALL
agent-plugin/tests/run.sh                        test-w-run-timeout.sh
agent-plugin/tests/affected.map                  ALL
agent-plugin/tests/hyper                         ALL
